{"subjectId":"sql","id":"null-handling","title":"NULL & Three-Valued Logic","group":"Querying Basics","order":18,"html":"<p class=\"lead\"><code>NULL</code> means <em>unknown / missing</em>. It is not zero, not an empty string, and not equal to anything — not even another <code>NULL</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--def\"><p><strong>Three-valued logic</strong> — SQL conditions evaluate to <code>TRUE</code>, <code>FALSE</code> or <code>UNKNOWN</code>. Any comparison with <code>NULL</code> (<code>=</code>, <code>&lt;&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;</code>…) is <code>UNKNOWN</code>, and <code>WHERE</code> keeps only <code>TRUE</code> rows.</p></div>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-equal-not\"></i>Comparisons with NULL</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"sql\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>SQL</figcaption><pre><code>SELECT NULL = NULL      AS eq,\n       NULL &lt;&gt; 1        AS ne,\n       NULL IS NULL     AS is_null,\n       1 IS NOT NULL    AS is_not_null,\n       NULL + 5         AS arithmetic,\n       'a' || NULL      AS concat;</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>eq   | ne   | is_null | is_not_null | arithmetic | concat\n-----+------+---------+-------------+------------+-------\nNULL | NULL | 1       | 1           | NULL       | NULL</code></pre></figure>\n<p>(SQLite shows <code>TRUE</code>/<code>FALSE</code> as <code>1</code>/<code>0</code> and <code>UNKNOWN</code> as <code>NULL</code>.) <code>NULL</code> propagates through arithmetic and concatenation — one missing value makes the whole expression <code>NULL</code>.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"sql\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>SQL</figcaption><pre><code>SELECT name FROM employees WHERE email = NULL;        -- always empty!\nSELECT name FROM employees WHERE email IS NULL ORDER BY name;</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>name\n----\n\nname\n----\nDev\nNeha</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-table\"></i>Truth tables</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th><code>AND</code></th><th>TRUE</th><th>FALSE</th><th>UNKNOWN</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>TRUE</strong></td><td>TRUE</td><td>FALSE</td><td>UNKNOWN</td></tr><tr><td><strong>FALSE</strong></td><td>FALSE</td><td>FALSE</td><td>FALSE</td></tr><tr><td><strong>UNKNOWN</strong></td><td>UNKNOWN</td><td>FALSE</td><td>UNKNOWN</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th><code>OR</code></th><th>TRUE</th><th>FALSE</th><th>UNKNOWN</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>TRUE</strong></td><td>TRUE</td><td>TRUE</td><td>TRUE</td></tr><tr><td><strong>FALSE</strong></td><td>TRUE</td><td>FALSE</td><td>UNKNOWN</td></tr><tr><td><strong>UNKNOWN</strong></td><td>TRUE</td><td>UNKNOWN</td><td>UNKNOWN</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><code>NOT UNKNOWN</code> is still <code>UNKNOWN</code>. So a row with a <code>NULL</code> column fails <em>both</em> <code>x = 5</code> and <code>NOT (x = 5)</code>:</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"sql\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>SQL</figcaption><pre><code>SELECT COUNT(*) AS total,\n       SUM(dept_id = 1)                   AS in_eng,\n       SUM(NOT (dept_id = 1))             AS not_in_eng,\n       SUM(dept_id IS NULL)               AS no_dept\nFROM employees;</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>total | in_eng | not_in_eng | no_dept\n------+--------+------------+--------\n10    | 4      | 5          | 1</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-alert-triangle\"></i>The NOT IN trap</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"sql\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>SQL</figcaption><pre><code>-- customers outside Mumbai and Delhi (Kavya's city is NULL)\nSELECT name FROM customers WHERE city NOT IN ('Mumbai', 'Delhi') ORDER BY name;\nSELECT 'x' AS found WHERE 3 NOT IN (1, 2, NULL);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>name\n-----\nSneha\n\nfound\n-----</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p><code>x NOT IN (1, 2, NULL)</code> is never true: it means <code>x &lt;&gt; 1 AND x &lt;&gt; 2 AND x &lt;&gt; NULL</code>, and the last part is unknown. If a <code>NOT IN (subquery)</code> can return a <code>NULL</code>, the whole query returns nothing. Use <code>NOT EXISTS</code> instead (see Semi &amp; Anti Joins). Also note Kavya (city <code>NULL</code>) is missing from the first result.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-tool\"></i>NULL-handling functions</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Returns</th><th>Portability</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>COALESCE(a, b, c…)</code></td><td>First non-<code>NULL</code> argument</td><td>Standard — everywhere</td></tr><tr><td><code>NULLIF(a, b)</code></td><td><code>NULL</code> if <code>a = b</code>, else <code>a</code></td><td>Standard — everywhere</td></tr><tr><td><code>IFNULL(a, b)</code></td><td><code>b</code> if <code>a</code> is <code>NULL</code></td><td>MySQL, SQLite</td></tr><tr><td><code>ISNULL(a, b)</code> / <code>NVL(a, b)</code></td><td>Same idea</td><td>SQL Server / Oracle</td></tr><tr><td><code>a IS DISTINCT FROM b</code></td><td>Null-safe <code>&lt;&gt;</code> (<code>NULL</code> vs <code>NULL</code> → false)</td><td>Standard; PostgreSQL, SQL Server 2022, SQLite (<code>IS NOT</code>)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"sql\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>SQL</figcaption><pre><code>SELECT name,\n       COALESCE(email, 'no email')          AS contact,\n       COALESCE(dept_id, 0)                 AS dept\nFROM employees\nWHERE emp_id IN (6, 7, 10)\nORDER BY emp_id;\n\n-- NULLIF avoids division by zero: x / 0 → x / NULL → NULL\nSELECT 100 / NULLIF(0, 0) AS safe_div;\n\n-- null-safe equality (SQLite: IS / IS NOT; standard: IS [NOT] DISTINCT FROM)\nSELECT NULL IS NULL AS both_null, 1 IS NOT NULL AS differ, NULL IS 1 AS null_vs_1;</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>name  | contact       | dept\n------+---------------+-----\nArjun | arjun@corp.in | 2\nNeha  | no email      | 2\nDev   | no email      | 0\n\nsafe_div\n--------\nNULL\n\nboth_null | differ | null_vs_1\n----------+--------+----------\n1         | 1      | 0</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list-check\"></i>NULL in aggregates, sorting and grouping</h3>\n<ul><li>Aggregates <strong>ignore</strong> <code>NULL</code>s: <code>COUNT(email)</code> counts non-null emails; <code>AVG</code> divides by the non-null count.</li><li><code>COUNT(*)</code> counts rows, whatever they contain.</li><li><code>GROUP BY</code> and <code>DISTINCT</code> put all <code>NULL</code>s into <strong>one</strong> group.</li><li><code>ORDER BY</code> puts <code>NULL</code>s first or last depending on the engine.</li><li><code>UNIQUE</code> allows multiple <code>NULL</code>s (except SQL Server).</li></ul>\n<figure data-lang=\"sql\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>SQL</figcaption><pre><code>SELECT COUNT(*) AS all_rows, COUNT(email) AS with_email, COUNT(dept_id) AS with_dept\nFROM employees;</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>all_rows | with_email | with_dept\n---------+------------+----------\n10       | 8          | 9</code></pre></figure>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What is the difference between NULL, 0 and an empty string?</summary><div><p><code>0</code> and <code>''</code> are known values that compare and sort normally. <code>NULL</code> is the absence of a value: comparisons with it yield <code>UNKNOWN</code>, it is skipped by aggregates and needs <code>IS NULL</code>. (Oracle is odd: it treats <code>''</code> as <code>NULL</code>.)</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Why does WHERE col &lt;&gt; 'x' not return rows where col is NULL?</summary><div><p><code>NULL &lt;&gt; 'x'</code> is <code>UNKNOWN</code>, and <code>WHERE</code> keeps only <code>TRUE</code>. Write <code>WHERE col &lt;&gt; 'x' OR col IS NULL</code>, or <code>WHERE col IS DISTINCT FROM 'x'</code>.</p></div></details></section>"}